@* helsedata's page shell, reduced to the parts that are hostile to a mounted component, and
   copied structurally from their own Features/SiteLayout/Views/_Layout.cshtml.

   Two things make this host different from samples/LegacyHost and samples/ModernHost, and both
   are the reason four layout defects reached a branch on 2026-09-03 having passed 1317 unit
   tests and eight axe states (Fhi.Metadata-l9l2n.40):

   1. THE STYLESHEET IS THEIRS. Not a stand-in that styles the same class names — the real
      Fhi.Helsedata.Stiler package, at the same _content path their layout links. It carries a
      bare `div { display: block }` (main.css, in the normalise block), and an author rule beats
      the browser's own `[hidden] { display: none }`: a `hidden` panel stayed on screen here and
      nowhere else, 3798px of it. It also gives `.munin-explorer` a
      `display: grid; grid-template-columns: 384px minmax(0, 1fr)` above 1024px, which is what
      turned a nested view wearing that class into two columns of scattered controls.

      Neither of those can be synthesised. A hand-written header reproduces neither.

   2. THE HEADER IS OVER THE CONTENT, NOT ABOVE IT. `.main-header` is
      `position: absolute; top: 0` with a 64px `.main-header__content` inside it, so it occupies
      no space in flow and the page's first 64px are underneath it. Every other sample starts the
      component at a clean y=0 with nothing over it; the real host does not, and the tablist
      rendered at document top 0 was invisible there for exactly that reason.

   Deliberately NOT copied from their layout: the CMS plumbing, the skip links, Matomo, the
   footer, the fonts from Google. None of it changes the geometry, and each is another thing to
   go stale. What is here is the shell, the header and the content wrapper. *@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="no">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>@ViewData["Title"] — Munin Explorer hostile host</title>

    @* The one line this whole sample exists for. Their layout links exactly this. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/_content/Fhi.Helsedata.Stiler/css/main.css" />
</head>
<body>
    <div id="wrapper">
        <div class="pagetopbg"></div>

        <header class="main-header">
            <div class="page-container">
                <div class="main-header__content">
                    <div class="main-header__content__container">
                        <span class="main-header__content__logo">helsedata.no (stand-in chrome)</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </header>

        <div class="wrapper">
            <div class="contentwrapper">
                <main id="maincontent">
                    @RenderBody()
                </main>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* Legacy Blazor Server: blazor.server.js, not blazor.web.js — the same as helsedata. *@
    <script src="_framework/blazor.server.js"></script>
    @await RenderSectionAsync("Scripts", required: false)
</body>
</html>
